  "notable_quotes": [
    "Prior MOFs often show a capacity-selectivity trade-off: some have high C3H6 uptake but only moderate selectivity, while others are selective but load little C3H6.",
    "Mn-dtzip is highly porous after solvent removal, with 65.8% porosity, an effective pore size of about 12.4 Å, and BET area of 880.9 m2 g-1.",
    "Mn-dtzip combines open metal sites with uncoordinated tetrazolate N and carboxylate O sites, creating more accessible C3H6 binding sites than for C2H4."
